{"id":"mahabharata-3-077","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":77,"title":"सप्तसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 77 · Nala wins back his kingdom","summary":{"en":"After a month Nala returns to Nishadha with a small escort and challenges Pushkara to a game, staking himself and Damayanti against the kingdom. Now master of the dice, he wins everything back at a single throw, forgives his brother and sends him home with wealth.","kn":"ಒಂದು ತಿಂಗಳ ನಂತರ ನಳನು ಸಣ್ಣ ಪರಿವಾರದೊಂದಿಗೆ ನಿಷಧಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳಿ ತನ್ನನ್ನೂ ದಮಯಂತಿಯನ್ನೂ ರಾಜ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಎದುರಾಗಿ ಪಣವಿಟ್ಟು ಪುಷ್ಕರನನ್ನು ಜೂಜಿಗೆ ಕರೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಈಗ ಅಕ್ಷನಿಪುಣನಾದ ಅವನು ಒಂದೇ ದಾಳದಲ್ಲಿ ಎಲ್ಲವನ್ನೂ ಮರಳಿ ಗೆದ್ದು ಸಹೋದರನನ್ನು ಕ್ಷಮಿಸಿ ಧನದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"एक महीने बाद नल छोटे दल के साथ निषध लौटकर पुष्कर को द्यूत की चुनौती देते हैं और राज्य के विरुद्ध स्वयं को और दमयन्ती को दाँव पर लगाते हैं। अब अक्ष-निपुण नल एक ही फेंक में सब वापस जीत लेते हैं, भाई को क्षमा कर धन सहित विदा करते हैं।","te":"ఒక నెల తర్వాత నలుడు చిన్న పరివారంతో నిషధానికి తిరిగివచ్చి రాజ్యానికి ఎదురుగా తనను, దమయంతిని పణంగా పెట్టి పుష్కరుని జూదానికి సవాలు చేస్తాడు. ఇప్పుడు అక్షనిపుణుడైన అతడు ఒక్క వేటుకే అంతా తిరిగి గెలిచి సోదరుని క్షమించి ధనంతో పంపివేస్తాడు.","ta":"ஒரு மாதம் கழித்து நளன் சிறு படையுடன் நிஷதத்துக்குத் திரும்பி, அரசுக்கு எதிராகத் தன்னையும் தமயந்தியையும் பந்தயம் வைத்துப் புஷ்கரனைச் சூதுக்கு அழைக்கிறான். இப்போது பகடையில் வல்லவனான அவன் ஒரே உருட்டில் அனைத்தையும் மீட்டு, சகோதரனை மன்னித்துச் செல்வத்துடன் அனுப்புகிறான்.","ml":"ഒരു മാസം കഴിഞ്ഞ് നളൻ ചെറിയ പരിവാരവുമായി നിഷധത്തിലേക്ക് മടങ്ങി, പുഷ്കരനെ ചൂതുകളിക്ക് വെല്ലുവിളിക്കുന്നു; രാജ്യത്തിനെതിരെ സ്വയവും ദമയന്തിയെയും പണയംവെക്കുന്നു. ഇപ്പോൾ ചൂതിൽ വിദഗ്ധനായ അദ്ദേഹം ഒറ്റ എറിയിൽത്തന്നെ എല്ലാം തിരിച്ചുപിടിക്കുന്നു; സഹോദരനോട് ക്ഷമിച്ച് സമ്പത്ത് നൽകി അയക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.77; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स मासमुष्य कौन्तेय भीममामन्त्र्य नैषधः ।\nपुरादल्पपरीवारो जगाम निषधान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, after staying a month, Nala took leave of Bhima and left the city with only a small retinue, heading for Nishadha."}},{"n":2,"text":"रथेनैकेन शुभ्रेण दन्तिभिः परिषोडशैः ।\nपञ्चाशद्भिर्हयैश्चैव षट्शतैश्च पदातिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went with one gleaming chariot, sixteen elephants, fifty horses and six hundred foot soldiers."}},{"n":3,"text":"स कम्पयन्निव महीं त्वरमाणो महीपतिः ।\nप्रविवेशातिसंरब्धस्तरसैव महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hurrying, that high-souled king, filled with fierce energy, entered his land as though shaking the earth."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः पुष्करमासाद्य वीरसेनसुतो नलः ।\nउवाच दीव्याव पुनर्बहु वित्तं मयार्जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Nala, son of Virasena, reached Pushkara and said, \"Let us gamble again. I have won great wealth."}},{"n":5,"text":"दमयन्ती च यच्चान्यन्मया वसु समर्जितम् ।\nएष वै मम संन्यासस्तव राज्यं तु पुष्कर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Damayanti and whatever other riches I have gathered are my stake, and your kingdom, Pushkara, is yours."}},{"n":6,"text":"पुनः प्रवर्ततां द्यूतमिति मे निश्चिता मतिः ।\nएकपाणेन भद्रं ते प्राणयोश्च पणावहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have firmly decided: let the dice be played again. Good luck to you. With a single stake, let us wager our very lives."}},{"n":7,"text":"जित्वा परस्वमाहृत्य राज्यं वा यदि वा वसु ।\nप्रतिपाणः प्रदातव्यः परं हि धनमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who has won another's property, whether kingdom or wealth, must give the chance of a return stake, for that is called the highest rule."}},{"n":8,"text":"न चेद्वाञ्छसि तद्द्यूतं युद्धद्यूतं प्रवर्तताम् ।\nद्वैरथेनास्तु वै शान्तिस्तव वा मम वा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you do not want that game, let a contest of arms be the game. Let our quarrel be settled by a duel of chariots, yours or mine, O king."}},{"n":9,"text":"वंशभोज्यमिदं राज्यं मार्गितव्यं यथा तथा ।\nयेन तेनाप्युपायेन वृद्धानामिति शासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kingdom is an ancestral possession and must be claimed by whatever means; so the elders have taught."}},{"n":10,"text":"द्वयोरेकतरे बुद्धिः क्रियतामद्य पुष्कर ।\nकैतवेनाक्षवत्यां वा युद्धे वा नम्यतां धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Choose today one of the two, Pushkara: play at dice by trickery, or bend your bow in battle.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"नैषधेनैवमुक्तस्तु पुष्करः प्रहसन्निव ।\nध्रुवमात्मजयं मत्वा प्रत्याह पृथिवीपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus by Nala, Pushkara, laughing as it were, and sure of his own victory, answered the king."}},{"n":12,"text":"दिष्ट्या त्वयार्जितं वित्तं प्रतिपाणाय नैषध ।\nदिष्ट्या च दुष्कृतं कर्म दमयन्त्याः क्षयं गतम् ।\nदिष्ट्या च ध्रियसे राजन्सदारोऽरिनिबर्हण ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is lucky that you have won wealth to stake against me, Nala, and lucky that Damayanti's misfortune has ended. And lucky that you live, with your wife, O slayer of foes."}},{"n":13,"text":"धनेनानेन वैदर्भी जितेन समलंकृता ।\nमामुपस्थास्यति व्यक्तं दिवि शक्रमिवाप्सराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you are defeated, Vaidarbhi, decked with this wealth, will surely wait on me like an apsara serving Indra in heaven."}},{"n":14,"text":"नित्यशो हि स्मरामि त्वां प्रतीक्षामि च नैषध ।\nदेवने च मम प्रीतिर्न भवत्यसुहृद्गणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think of you every day, Nala, and I have been waiting; for I take no pleasure in gambling with mere unfriendly crowds."}},{"n":15,"text":"जित्वा त्वद्य वरारोहां दमयन्तीमनिन्दिताम् ।\nकृतकृत्यो भविष्यामि सा हि मे नित्यशो हृदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By winning the fair-hipped and blameless Damayanti today I shall be fulfilled, for she is always in my heart.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु तस्य ता वाचो बह्वबद्धप्रलापिनः ।\nइयेष स शिरश्छेत्तुं खड्गेन कुपितो नलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these many foolish words of his, Nala grew angry and wanted to cut off his head with his sword."}},{"n":17,"text":"स्मयंस्तु रोषताम्राक्षस्तमुवाच ततो नृपः ।\nपणावः किं व्याहरसे जित्वा वै व्याहरिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smiling, his eyes red with rage, the king said, \"Let us stake. Why do you babble? Babble after you have won.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः प्रावर्तत द्यूतं पुष्करस्य नलस्य च ।\nएकपाणेन भद्रं ते नलेन स पराजितः ।\nसरत्नकोशनिचयः प्राणेन पणितोऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the gambling between Pushkara and Nala began. With a single stake, good luck to you, Nala defeated him, and he lost his treasury of jewels and even his life, which had been staked."}},{"n":19,"text":"जित्वा च पुष्करं राजा प्रहसन्निदमब्रवीत् ।\nमम सर्वमिदं राज्यमव्यग्रं हतकण्टकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having beaten Pushkara, the king laughed and said, \"This whole kingdom is now mine, undisturbed and free of thorns."}},{"n":20,"text":"वैदर्भी न त्वया शक्या राजापसद वीक्षितुम् ।\nतस्यास्त्वं सपरीवारो मूढ दासत्वमागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, lowest of kings, are not fit even to look at Vaidarbhi. Fool, you and your household have become her slaves."}},{"n":21,"text":"न तत्त्वया कृतं कर्म येनाहं निर्जितः पुरा ।\nकलिना तत्कृतं कर्म त्वं तु मूढ न बुध्यसे ।\nनाहं परकृतं दोषं त्वय्याधास्ये कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was not you who did what once defeated me. Kali did it, and you, fool, do not understand. I will never lay another's fault on you."}},{"n":22,"text":"यथासुखं त्वं जीवस्व प्राणानभ्युत्सृजामि ते ।\nतथैव च मम प्रीतिस्त्वयि वीर न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Live as you please. I grant you your life. My affection for you remains, brave one, without doubt."}},{"n":23,"text":"सौभ्रात्रं चैव मे त्वत्तो न कदाचित्प्रहास्यति ।\nपुष्कर त्वं हि मे भ्राता संजीवस्व शतं समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My brotherly love for you will never leave me. Pushkara, you are my brother. Live a hundred years.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं नलः सान्त्वयित्वा भ्रातरं सत्यविक्रमः ।\nस्वपुरं प्रेषयामास परिष्वज्य पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus comforting his brother, Nala, true to his word, embraced him again and again and sent him to his own city."}},{"n":25,"text":"सान्त्वितो नैषधेनैवं पुष्करः प्रत्युवाच तम् ।\nपुण्यश्लोकं तदा राजन्नभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Comforted by the lord of Nishadha, Pushkara bowed to Nala of holy fame with folded hands and replied, O king."}},{"n":26,"text":"कीर्तिरस्तु तवाक्षय्या जीव वर्षायुतं सुखी ।\nयो मे वितरसि प्राणानधिष्ठानं च पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"May your fame never perish. Live ten thousand years in happiness, you who give me my life and a place to live, O king.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"स तथा सत्कृतो राज्ञा मासमुष्य तदा नृपः ।\nप्रययौ स्वपुरं हृष्टः पुष्करः स्वजनावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoured so by Nala, Pushkara stayed there a month, then went joyfully to his own city, surrounded by his people."}},{"n":28,"text":"महत्या सेनया राजन्विनीतैः परिचारकैः ।\nभ्राजमान इवादित्यो वपुषा पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a great army and well-trained attendants, O best of men, he shone in body like the sun."}},{"n":29,"text":"प्रस्थाप्य पुष्करं राजा वित्तवन्तमनामयम् ।\nप्रविवेश पुरं श्रीमानत्यर्थमुपशोभितम् ।\nप्रविश्य सान्त्वयामास पौरांश्च निषधाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having sent off Pushkara, prosperous and unharmed, the glorious king entered his city, splendidly decorated, and there the lord of Nishadha comforted the citizens."}}]}]}